Privacy Policy
Rise
Effective date: 24 October 2026

1. Who we are (controller)
Peter Švorc (“we”, “us”), Slovakia, is the controller of personal data processed in connection with the Rise app.

Contact for privacy requests: support@bots5lab.com

We do not publish a postal address in this Policy. You can contact us by email for any privacy matter.

2. Scope
This Policy describes how Rise handles information when you use the iOS app. It applies alongside our Terms of Use.

3. What Rise is
Rise is a wake-up / morning-routine app (alarms, soundscapes, optional light waking, challenges, insights, widgets, and Live Activities). This version is free and does not include in-app purchases.

4. Data we process
A. Data stored on your device (generally not uploaded to our servers)
Depending on what you enter and use:

name / display name
alarm and bedtime settings, repeat days, sound preferences, challenge settings
light-waking preference
notes (e.g. “tomorrow” notes)
onboarding answers (e.g. sleep length, how you feel on waking)
local wake history, streaks, and similar insights data
app preferences (appearance, tutorials completed, review flags)
This data is stored locally (including in an App Group so widgets / extensions can read what they need). We do not require a Rise account.

B. Analytics we send to our servers
We collect anonymous product analytics to understand how Rise is used and improve it.
Analytics are only collected after you agree to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy in the app, and only on production App Store installs (not TestFlight / Xcode). You can turn collection off anytime under Settings → Share anonymous analytics.

Typically includes:

a random device identifier (UUID generated on device)
event names (examples: app open, onboarding steps, alarm/sleep events, review-prompt events)
limited event properties (e.g. toggle states, app version)
timestamps
Analytics are sent to Supabase infrastructure hosted in the EU.

We design analytics not to include your name, tomorrow note text, or precise GPS location.

C. Purchases
This version of Rise does not offer in-app purchases. We do not process payments or purchase history through the App.

D. Permissions-related data (device OS)
With your permission, the system may allow Rise to use:

Notifications — schedule local alerts
Camera — flashlight only for light waking (not for uploading photos/video)
Background audio — play audible wake ambience during gradual wake (microphone is never used; Rise does not record audio)
Live Activities — show sleep/wake status on system UI
optionally system alarm features if available
Permission status itself may be checked on device to operate features.

E. What we do not do
We do not sell your personal data.
We do not use your data for third-party advertising networks.
We do not require you to create an email/password Rise account for core use.

