6. Children
Rise is for a general audience. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children for commercial profiling.

If you believe a child provided data inappropriately, contact support@bots5lab.com and we will take reasonable steps to delete analytics linked to a device ID you help us identify.

Parents/guardians should supervise use by minors and manage Apple Screen Time settings as appropriate.

7. Sharing / processors
We share data only as needed with:

Apple — App Store, push/local notification delivery, OS features
Supabase — EU hosting for analytics
These providers process data on our instructions or as independent controllers for their own platform services (especially Apple).

We do not sell personal data and do not share it with advertisers for targeted ads.

8. International transfers
Analytics are hosted in the EU. Apple may process data in other countries under their terms and safeguards. Where required, transfers rely on appropriate mechanisms (e.g. Standard Contractual Clauses) used by those providers.

9. Retention
On-device data: until you delete it in-app (where available), clear app data, or uninstall Rise (subject to OS backups you control).
Analytics events: retained for a limited operational period (raw events are not kept indefinitely; we aim for roughly 90 days for raw event detail unless we state otherwise).
Aggregated statistics: we may keep de-identified or aggregated metrics (not tied to your device ID) to understand long-term product trends.
10. Your choices and rights
In the App
Change or delete many local settings yourself
Settings → Remove my analytics data — deletes analytics events associated with your device ID from our analytics tables (aggregate totals may remain without your device ID)
Settings → Share anonymous analytics — turn off to stop future analytics collection
Manage notifications, camera, and other permissions in iOS Settings
GDPR rights (EU/EEA/UK as applicable)
You may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection, and portability where applicable, and you may lodge a complaint with your supervisory authority (in Slovakia, the Úrad na ochranu osobných údajov SR).

Because Rise is largely local-first and analytics are device-ID based, we may ask you for information needed to locate your analytics device ID.

Contact: support@bots5lab.com

“Do Not Sell”
We do not sell personal information as that term is commonly used under CCPA/CPRA. If that changes, we will update this Policy.

11. Security
We use reasonable technical and organizational measures appropriate to a small consumer app (including limiting analytics content and using infrastructure access controls). No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure.

12. Sharing features
If you use share sheets (e.g. Insights images), the content is shared by you through Apple’s share UI to destinations you choose. We do not operate those destination services.

13. Widgets, App Group, Live Activities
Data needed for widgets and Live Activities may be shared on-device between the main app and extensions via Apple App Group storage. This stays on your device unless a feature explicitly sends data to our servers (analytics as described above).

14. Changes
We may update this Privacy Policy. The Effective date will be updated. For material changes, we may provide additional notice in the App when practical.

